---
/**
 * Privacy policy (English). A translation of src/pages/privacy.astro: keep the two in sync, the Hebrew is the source.
 * Not legal advice: have a lawyer review it. Lines marked TODO confirm follow the same open items as the Hebrew page.
 */
import PrivacyShell from "../../components/pages/PrivacyShell.astro";
import { SITE, contactLink } from "../../config/site";
const updated = "November 17, 2026";
---

<PrivacyShell description="What information Tadam! collects, why, who it is shared with and what your rights are." updatedLine={`Last updated: ${updated}`}>

  <p class="lead">
    Tadam! creates live trivia games for events, from the stories and photos you send us. This policy explains what
    information we collect, what we use it for, who it is shared with and what your rights are. Your photos and stories
    stay yours.
  </p>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#collect">What information we collect</a></li>
      <li><a href="#use">What we use the information for</a></li>
      <li><a href="#share">Who the information is shared with</a></li>
      <li><a href="#others">Information about other people and children</a></li>
      <li><a href="#keep">How long we keep the information</a></li>
      <li><a href="#rights">Your rights</a></li>
      <li><a href="#security">Information security</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact us</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section id="collect">
    <h2 class="display">1. What information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>When you leave your details on the site:</strong> name, phone number, type of event and approximate date, if you filled it in.</li>
      <li><strong>When you contact us on Messenger or by email:</strong> your name and Facebook profile or your email address, and the content of the messages.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>The materials for the game:</strong> stories, questions, photos and details about the guests of honor and
        the guests, which you choose to send us so we can build the game.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>During the game at the event:</strong> guests join from their phones by scanning a code, choose a display
        name and answer the questions. The name and the score appear on the screen and on the leaderboard.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical information:</strong> like any website, the hosting servers log basic technical information
        (such as IP address and browser type) to run the site and keep it secure. At the moment the site does not use
        advertising tools or third-party tracking.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="use">
    <h2 class="display">2. What we use the information for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To get back to you, answer questions and coordinate the event.</li>
      <li>To build your game and run it at the event.</li>
      <li>To improve the service and keep the site secure.</li>
    </ul>
    {/* TODO confirm: the same commitments as the FAQ answer "Who sees the photos and stories?" */}
    <p>
      We do not sell your information, we do not use your photos and stories for advertising without your explicit
      approval, and we do not use them to train AI models.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="share">
    <h2 class="display">3. Who the information is shared with</h2>
    <p>
      Only you and we see your materials before the event. At the event itself, the game is shown on the big screen and
      on the phones of the guests who are playing. To provide the service we work with providers, who receive only what
      they need:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Netlify:</strong> hosting the site and receiving the forms you fill in on it.</li>
      <li><strong>Meta (Facebook and Messenger) and Google (Gmail):</strong> our conversations and correspondence with you.</li>
      <li><strong>The game platform:</strong> the service where the game is built and runs at the event, including the questions and photos in it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of the providers store information on servers outside Israel. We will hand information to another party only
      if the law requires us to.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="others">
    <h2 class="display">4. Information about other people and children</h2>
    <p>
      The game is built from stories and photos of the guests of honor and of people close to them, sometimes children
      too (for example at a birthday or a bar or bat mitzvah). When you send us materials about other people, you
      confirm that you are allowed to share them for the game. We use them only for the game of your event, and we
      recommend not sending sensitive information such as medical information or ID numbers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="keep">
    <h2 class="display">5. How long we keep the information</h2>
    {/* TODO confirm: retention. No automatic-deletion promise until the real policy is decided. */}
    <p>
      We keep the information for as long as it is needed for the purposes it was collected for, for example so the
      game stays with you as a keepsake after the event. You can ask us at any time to delete your materials and your
      contact details, and we will handle the request promptly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rights">
    <h2 class="display">6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the Israeli Privacy Protection Law, you can:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask to see the information we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Ask us to correct wrong information or to delete information.</li>
      <li>Ask us not to contact you anymore.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise these rights, write to us at the address at the end of this page.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2 class="display">7. Information security</h2>
    <p>
      We take reasonable measures to protect your information, and access to it is limited to those who need it to
      provide you with the service. No method guarantees complete protection, and if we discover that your information
      was compromised we will let you know.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2 class="display">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of the page shows when it was last updated.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2 class="display">9. Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions, requests or comments about your privacy? Write to us:</p>
    <ul class="contact">
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
      <li>Messenger: <a href={contactLink("privacy")} target="_blank" rel="noopener">the Tadam! Facebook page</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</PrivacyShell>
